## Path-scoped rules

Match the file you are editing to the rule that governs it. Read the rule
before editing, not after:

| When editing | Read |
|---|---|
| gameplay systems | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/gameplay-code.md` |
| engine-layer code | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/engine-code.md` |
| AI / behaviour | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/ai-code.md` |
| networking | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/network-code.md` |
| shaders | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/shader-code.md` |
| UI | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/ui-code.md` |
| prototypes | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/prototype-code.md` |
| tests | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/test-standards.md` |
| design documents | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/design-docs.md` |
| narrative | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/narrative.md` |
| data files | `{{CONTENT_DIR}}rules/data-files.md` |

This harness does not load these automatically — there is no path-scoped
rule mechanism. The table is the mechanism.

## How this studio works

Load `gs-studio` for the operating system, `gs-roster` before delegating,
`gs-pipeline` to find the current phase, and `gs-guards` before committing.

## Collaborative, not autonomous

Present options and trade-offs; the user decides. Do not start
implementation on an unapproved design.
